# llmEngineering2.0

## Overview

**llmEngineering2.0** is a hands-on learning and experimentation repository focused on building modern **Large Language Model (LLM)** and **Generative AI (GenAI)** systems. The goal of this repo is to move from fundamentals to practical, production-oriented AI workflows.

This repository emphasizes *understanding first, scale later* — focusing on clear concepts, clean implementations, and real-world system design.

---

## What This Repository Covers

* **PyTorch** fundamentals and deep learning workflows
* **Transformers & LLMs** (from basics to practical usage)
* **Generative AI** concepts and applications
* **RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation)** systems
* **Agentic AI** and tool-using LLM agents
* **FastAPI** for serving AI models and APIs
* **MCP (Model / Multi-Component Pipelines)** concepts and experiments

---

## Learning Philosophy

* Start from **core fundamentals** (tensors, autograd, attention)
* Build things **from scratch before using abstractions**
* Prefer **clarity over shortcuts**
* Use **small models locally**, scale using cloud when needed

This repo is structured as a **learning + project notebook**, not just finished demos.

---

## Repository Structure (High-Level)

```text
llmEngineering2.0/
│
├── pytorch/          # PyTorch fundamentals (tensors, autograd, nn.Module)
├── transformers/    # Transformer blocks and attention mechanisms
├── llms/             # Language models and text generation
├── rags/             # Retrieval-Augmented Generation pipelines
├── agents/           # Agentic AI, tools, planning, memory
├── fastapi/          # Serving models and APIs with FastAPI
├── genai/            # Generative AI experiments and applications
└── projects/         # End-to-end mini and capstone projects
```

(The structure may evolve as the repository grows.)

---

## Tools & Technologies

* **PyTorch**
* **Hugging Face Transformers & Datasets**
* **LangChain / Agent frameworks**
* **FastAPI & Uvicorn**
* **FAISS / Vector databases**
* **Jupyter Notebooks**

---

## Hardware & Execution Strategy

* **Local machine:**

  * CPU-based PyTorch
  * Small-scale experiments
  * Concept validation

* **Cloud (e.g., Colab/Kaggle):**

  * LLM fine-tuning
  * RAG pipelines
  * Heavier GenAI workloads

---

## Who This Repo Is For

* Learners transitioning from **ML/DL to LLMs & GenAI**
* Developers interested in **LLM engineering and AI systems**
* Anyone who wants a **structured, practical path** into modern AI

